    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d368">

                <pb facs="0510" n="406" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg406"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.911/16.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 619.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-02-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 6, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my telegrams of February 6 (1
                    p.m. and 2 p.m.) in regard to abusive articles concerning the Legation published
                    in the newspaper “Cuba,” I have the honor to transmit herewith enclosed copies
                    and translations of the two articles in question.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d368-f1"
                    /> Judging from the tenor of the articles already published, it is to be
                    presumed that they will be followed by others of a similar nature.</p>
                <p>The Department is in possession of the facts concerning past offenses of this
                    newspaper in its attacks upon Mr. Gibson last August and upon the President at a
                    later date. I therefore deem it superfluous to enter into a discussion of the
                    matter, but venture to confirm my earnest recommendation already made that I be
                    authorized to present a formal request to the Cuban Government that action be
                    taken against this newspaper for criminal libel.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. M. Beaupré</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
